00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.680
Hey everyone I am Abbey Sharp welcome to another edition of Fertility Files here

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.189
at Abbey's Kitchen! Now, you may remember
that in some of my previous Fertility

00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:12.269
Files videos we talked about my personal
struggle with infertility in trying to

00:00:12.269 --> 00:00:16.830
get pregnant and that one of the major
issues that I had in my journey was that

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:21.240
my uterine lining just didn't thicken,
and that it was suggested that it was

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:25.590
possible that my long term use of the
birth control pill may have played a

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:32.340
role. I was on the pill for 14 years,
before which I had a totally normal

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:37.700
regular cycle but when I came off I just
never got a period. So based on your

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:43.230
overwhelming interest in this topic, I
wanted to dive deep into the research to

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:48.090
find out what the literature said about
the oral contraceptive use and long term

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:53.640
fertility. I also acknowledge that I am
NOT a doctor and I'm specifically not a

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:59.250
reproductive endocrinologist or a
gynecologist. So I am in no way giving

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:04.439
you any advice at all on your own use of
the birth control pill. I am however

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:09.450
trained and analyzing research, so what I
am planning to do today is to simply

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:15.659
regurgitate my findings as unbiased as I
possibly can and to bring you some

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:21.090
actual credible advice from some experts
in this unique field. So I'm going to be

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:25.350
joined by my reproductive
endocrinologist Dr. Tom Hannam from

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:31.110
Hannam Fertility Clinic in Toronto as
well as Mama Dr. Jones to get their take.

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:35.700
Now before we get into this of course I
want to remind you that the information

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:40.229
in this video is for educational and
entertaining purposes only and you

00:01:40.229 --> 00:01:44.700
should always speak to your doctor about
your unique healthcare case.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:49.409
Okay so let's kick things off by
answering an important introductory

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:55.290
question. How does the birth control pill
even work? Now the pill is an oral

00:01:55.290 --> 00:02:00.240
contraceptive that contains synthetic
estrogen and progestin, similar to the

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:03.899
hormones that naturally occur in a
woman's body, in order to trick the body

00:02:03.899 --> 00:02:08.729
into suppressing ovulation. This takes
place because the pituitary gland

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:13.730
produces follicle stimulating hormone,
which is FSH, which in turn

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:18.560
stimulates the production of estrogen
and progesterone which lastly encourages

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.290
ovulation.
Now the synthetic hormones make the

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:26.959
pituitary glands produce less FSH,
suppressing normal ovulation. The birth

00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:31.459
control pill also does a couple other
things to prevent unwanted pregnancy. The

00:02:31.459 --> 00:02:35.599
first is a thinning of the uterine
lining. Now a uterine lining of at least

00:02:35.599 --> 00:02:40.459
8 millimeters in thickness is really
important for maintaining pregnancy as

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:46.099
that is the lining that the fertilized
embryo can nestle into for implantation.

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:51.290
So to help prevent this from happening,
the pill depletes glycogen stores to

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:55.970
thin out the lining. The pill also may
thicken cervical mucus to prevent the

00:02:55.970 --> 00:03:00.859
sperm from reaching any of the eggs.
There's a lot going on in these teeny

00:03:00.859 --> 00:03:05.599
tiny little pills. Now does the pill
affect future fertility?

00:03:05.599 --> 00:03:11.510
If you speak to most doctors, most will
advise you that after a few cycles post

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:16.940
pill your body will return to its pre-pill state. In fact, a lot of the evidence

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:22.700
on contraceptive use and fertility is
actually quite reassuring. One study

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:26.630
found that 96.8% of
women got their period back within three

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:31.069
months after coming off the pill, and
another study found that after one year

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:35.959
of pill use 57% of women got
pregnant after three months and 81%

00:03:35.959 --> 00:03:40.040
got pregnant after 12 months.
There was even a study suggesting that

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:44.569
the longer women were on the pill, up to
five years, the greater their chances of

00:03:44.569 --> 00:03:50.120
conceiving. The rationale being that the
extended hormonal exposure may confer a

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:55.760
protective effect via minimization of
endometrial proliferation and menstrual

00:03:55.760 --> 00:04:01.040
shedding, which would help prevent
endometriosis or endometrial dysfunction.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:06.799
However, we do know that not all women
respond to medication the same and a few

00:04:06.799 --> 00:04:11.959
studies, as well as a lot of anecdotal
experiences, have found that there can be

00:04:11.959 --> 00:04:17.449
more significant delays in the return of
your period and ovulation which in turn

00:04:17.449 --> 00:04:22.250
may impact fertility. Now research has
found that the pill may disrupt normal

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:26.140
menstrual function
but the length of this disruption is

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:30.370
really what's up for debate.
One study found major cycle disturbances

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:35.320
after discontinuing oral contraceptives,
including cycle length changes with more

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:40.720
than 35 days in the luteal phase or anovulatory cycles for up to nine

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:44.920
months after discontinuing the pill.
Another prospective study on over a

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:48.970
thousand women who discontinued the pill
because they wanted to conceive, found

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:53.560
that the percentage of women who had
given birth after a year post-pill was

00:04:53.560 --> 00:05:00.040
about 32% for the pill 39%
percent for an IUD and 54% for

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:05.530
vaginal barrier methods. Interestingly,
while IUD users did fare better than the

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:09.940
pill users in the short-term, the
long-term use of the IUD seemed to

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:16.210
really impact fertility with only 28% of
women who had used the IUD for 78 months

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:21.550
or more getting pregnant and delivering
compared to 46% of short-term

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:26.980
users. Another study compared pill users
with non hormonal diaphragm users, and

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:32.650
found that after 12 months
70% of prior pill users had not yet

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:35.650
given birth
compared with 46% of women who

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:39.880
had used a diaphragm for contraception.
The difference between groups did seem

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:45.970
to disappear after about 42 months post
pill, but still three and a half years is

00:05:45.970 --> 00:05:51.669
a long time when you're desperately
trying to conceive. Finally, another study

00:05:51.669 --> 00:05:57.220
evaluating a variety of contraceptive
methods found that it took 25% of former

00:05:57.220 --> 00:06:01.750
pill users more than 13 months to
conceive after coming off the pill

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:09.940
compared to 12% and 8.5% of women using
IUDs and diaphragms, respectively. So the

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:14.710
research in this area as you can see is
clearly a mixed bag with some studies

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:18.669
finding no major differences in
contraceptive rates between pill users

00:06:18.669 --> 00:06:25.330
and non-pill users, and others uncovering
some sobering stats. It's very likely

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:29.830
that different women respond differently
to different drugs and there are a few

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:34.570
possible reasons why some women may
experience this fertility delay. Number

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:40.370
one, the pills impact on uterine lining.
First, let's revisit how the pill thins

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:44.060
the uterine lining. Now, because it's
ideal to have a thicker uterine lining

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:48.500
here, probably about eight to fourteen
millimeters when you're trying to

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:52.729
conceive, the birth control pill is
supposed to thin the uterine lining in

00:06:52.729 --> 00:06:57.380
hopes of preventing an unwanted
pregnancy. The question, however, is how

00:06:57.380 --> 00:07:02.270
long it takes for a woman's uterine
lining to begin to thicken again after

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:06.979
discontinuing the pill, and how would
this impact her future fertility?

00:07:06.979 --> 00:07:10.760
Well, while research in this area is
definitely in its infancy,

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:17.030
one study conducted in 2012 found that
long-term birth control pill use, about

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:22.880
five years or more, can potentially limit
the growth of the endometrial lining aka

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:26.960
the uterine lining. The study looked at a
138 patients and

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:31.370
found that those who had a uterine
lining thickness of seven millimeters or

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:36.560
thicker had a mean use of the birth
control pill of 5.8 years.

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:41.330
While those who had a thickness less
than seven millimeters, had a mean use of

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:46.160
9.8t years. In other words,
the longer you're on the pill the

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:50.539
potentially thinner the lining. Next,
let's consider the pills impact on

00:07:50.539 --> 00:07:55.460
cervical mucus. So another concern is the
fact that the pill thickens the cervical

00:07:55.460 --> 00:08:01.130
mucus to prevent sperm from getting up
there. Now how long does this last after

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:05.539
discontinuing the pill? Unfortunately, not
a whole lot of research has been done on

00:08:05.539 --> 00:08:10.639
this topic. However, one study claimed that
after discontinuation menstrual

00:08:10.639 --> 00:08:16.820
biomarkers such as length, intensity,
mucus score, and ovulation, were disturbed

00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:22.760
for about two cycles. After the two
cycles, the biomarkers researched seemed

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:27.500
to start to regulate themselves given
some time. Now the third, is the pills

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:32.029
impact on AMH levels. Now, it's very
common for women who are trying to

00:08:32.029 --> 00:08:38.750
conceive to get their anti-mullerian
hormone levels, aka AMH, tested to get an

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:43.130
idea of their overall fertility status.
AMH is used to check a woman's ability

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:47.209
to produce eggs that can be then
fertilized for pregnancy, where a higher

00:08:47.209 --> 00:08:50.630
AMH is related to better chances of
conception.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:55.550
One study found that after nine weeks of
using oral contraceptives, AMH levels

00:08:55.550 --> 00:09:00.920
decreased in all women tested. In another
study of 244 women that used oral

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:06.500
contraceptives, their AMH levels were 19% lower than women who didn't use

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:10.519
them.
Lastly, in another study, 228 women who

00:09:10.519 --> 00:09:15.920
used the pill had AMH levels lower than
women who didn't use it by almost a

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:21.050
third. Having said that, there have also
been a number of studies that state the

00:09:21.050 --> 00:09:26.480
complete opposite suggesting that the
pill did not have any effect on women's

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:32.300
AMH levels. Honestly, it's hard to say
whether or not oral contraceptives lower

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:38.360
AMH levels in all women or how long it
may take before they resume. But, it makes

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:43.550
sense to get tested a few months
following discontinuation of the pill to

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:48.740
get some accurate results. Now, finally, I
want to talk about the pills impact on

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:53.720
ovarian aging. Now, a lot of women who
struggle with fertility after being on

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:58.820
the pill are possibly diagnosed with
ovarian aging. Ovarian aging can make it

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:03.320
really difficult to conceive due to the
fact that the ovaries aren't receiving the

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:06.860
nutrients that they need to develop and
maintain a pregnancy.

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:14.240
These nutrients include coq10, vitamin E,
vitamin C, and selenium. In one study, it

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:18.529
was found that women who were on the
pill had lower levels of coq10 and

00:10:18.529 --> 00:10:23.209
vitamin E, compared to women who were not on the pill. Another study found that the

00:10:23.209 --> 00:10:30.310
pill may also deplete nutrient levels of
folic acid, vitamin b2, b6, b12, C, E,

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:36.680
magnesium, selenium, and zinc. And most of these are key players in reproductive

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:41.750
health. In fact, one study found that
low levels of coq10 is a common

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:46.880
association with infertility in women
due to low mitochondrial activity in the

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:50.810
ovarian oocytes. This can explain why
women experience delays in fertility

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:56.029
after being on the pill, without actually
having any pre-existing conditions.

00:10:56.029 --> 00:11:00.470
I also want to briefly touch on other
female health implications of the birth

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:06.440
control pill. Now in over 54 epidemiological
studies, over a hundred and fifty

00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:10.670
thousand women were studied as well as
the relationship between the birth

00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:15.890
control pill and breast cancer. Now, women
who had taken oral contraceptives in the

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:21.230
past had a 7% increase in the
risk of breast cancer, while women who

00:11:21.230 --> 00:11:24.770
were currently taking oral
contraceptives had a 24%

00:11:24.770 --> 00:11:28.970
increased risk. Another study found that
women who had taken the pill for over

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:35.150
five years, had a 10% increased risk for
cervical cancer and any longer it was

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:39.470
about a 60% increased risk. One
possible explanation for these findings

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:44.240
is that the synthetic hormones found in
the pill might increase the growth of

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:48.860
these cancers by binding to their
estrogen and/or progesterone receptors.

00:11:48.860 --> 00:11:54.170
Well, that's not all so great news. You
might be happy to know that other

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:59.510
research has found that women who had
taken the pill had a reduced risk of

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:05.420
endometrial cancer as the pills suppresses
endometrial cell growth. It may also help

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:10.160
reduce the risk of ovarian cancer by
decreasing the amount of ovulations a

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:14.660
woman experiences, which in turn,
decreases the exposure to naturally

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:19.910
occurring female hormones. But if the
pill isn't to blame for my infertility

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:25.910
then what exactly is? Now, there's no
denying that the hormones in the pill

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:31.430
may potentially impact short-term
fertility but there is also the

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:35.900
possibility that some women are
struggling with something else that was

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:40.640
sneakily present even before they
started the pill. It's very difficult to

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:45.200
link post-pill amenorrhea directly to
the pill always due to the fact that

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:50.120
about 1-2 women get diagnosed
with amenorrhea after coming off the pill

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:55.340
out of every hundred. So while the pill
may help regulate and manage PMS

00:12:55.340 --> 00:13:00.530
symptoms, it doesn't "cure" any
pre-existing conditions if present. It

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:06.320
only covers them up. So commonly masked
conditions include PCOS, hypothalamic

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:11.150
amenorrhea, and thyroid issues. And when
masking a conditioned for a prolonged

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:16.610
period of time, it can make it even more
difficult to regain your period

00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:21.230
or your fertility once you come off the
pill. So now that I have given you all

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:24.889
the research that I could find,
I want to loop in my reproductive

00:13:24.889 --> 00:13:30.829
endocrinologist Dr. Tom Hannam from Hannam Clinic here in Toronto. Okay so first

00:13:30.829 --> 00:13:36.499
question for you, in your clinical
experience does the long term use of the

00:13:36.499 --> 00:13:41.179
birth control pill impact women's
chances of conception and if so in

00:13:41.179 --> 00:13:43.694
your experience how does it do that?

00:13:43.694 --> 00:13:46.699
- The good news is for most women using birth

00:13:46.699 --> 00:13:50.839
control like birth
control pill, is not going to be

00:13:50.839 --> 00:13:54.980
consequential to their future
fertility. So women are positioned to be

00:13:54.980 --> 00:14:00.110
taking the pill, for example, comfortably.
For many women it actually makes for

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:04.129
easier cycles and confident that
their future selves will be able to

00:14:04.129 --> 00:14:08.029
achieve pregnancy afterwards. It's not
true for everybody, but it is true for

00:14:08.029 --> 00:14:11.600
most people.

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:12.889
- That is very
reassuring because, I mean, for a lot of

00:14:12.889 --> 00:14:17.779
women the birth control pill or any kind
of contraceptive is so important in

00:14:17.779 --> 00:14:18.279
their lifestyle so.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:23.899
- Right? So maybe someone might have started it a long time ago, maybe as a teenager

00:14:23.899 --> 00:14:27.439
because of pain, for example, or just trying to control regularity or of course for

00:14:27.439 --> 00:14:30.649
birth control. So for a lot of women
they've actually been on it for many

00:14:30.649 --> 00:14:33.619
years.
Interestingly during this time with covid

00:14:33.619 --> 00:14:38.600
a lot of family doctor groups,
chat groups, are talking about how many

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:41.419
women are extending their pills. So
people who have been thinking about

00:14:41.419 --> 00:14:45.049
trying to achieve pregnancy a lot of
people are putting  it off taking

00:14:45.049 --> 00:14:48.139
the pill for a bit longer or keeping
their IUD in place for a little bit

00:14:48.139 --> 00:14:51.499
longer. Just as they sort of watch and
figure out how everything's gonna settle

00:14:51.499 --> 00:14:55.759
out. So I could imagine there are a
number of people who would be watching

00:14:55.759 --> 00:15:00.679
your channel, both on the pill right now
and uncomfortable with the idea not wanting

00:15:00.679 --> 00:15:04.669
to get pregnant in this moment, but very
much hoping to be getting pregnant soon.

00:15:04.669 --> 00:15:09.769
Very interesting. So for
those women who may be affected by the

00:15:09.769 --> 00:15:14.200
pill, what is going on there that
may be causing those issues.

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:19.939
So the way the pill was designed was to be an estrogen, like your natural estrogen

00:15:19.939 --> 00:15:24.019
level, and naturally when your body
has lots of estrogen in the middle of

00:15:24.019 --> 00:15:28.009
the cycle it doesn't stimulate any eggs to
grow. So the idea behind the pill is,

00:15:28.009 --> 00:15:35.149
[inaudible]

00:15:35.149 --> 00:15:38.689
thats how it works. The thing is that
the estrogen is not your natural estrogen,

00:15:38.689 --> 00:15:41.060
of course.
It's called estrogen estradiol, it's a

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:44.329
synthetic estrogen and it actually works
differently for every woman,

00:15:44.329 --> 00:15:47.589
everyone's body, and it works differently
for different parts of their body.

00:15:47.589 --> 00:15:51.290
So, that's why, first of all, a lot of women
have to find the right pill for them

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:54.860
just to try to find the right dose that
works but that makes them feel kind of

00:15:54.860 --> 00:16:00.019
normal. But even then, it's never exactly
normal. It's never exactly what it would

00:16:00.019 --> 00:16:05.480
be naturally like to them with natural
estrogen levels. These estrogens actually,

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:10.160
interestingly, they work as positive
estrogens in some places and negative

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:14.269
estrogens in others. It's weird,
it's the way it binds to receptors.

00:16:14.269 --> 00:16:21.050
So for many women, it will, for example, take away hot flashes if a woman had a really

00:16:21.050 --> 00:16:24.079
naturally low estrogen level and takes
the pill, it should look better. That's a

00:16:24.079 --> 00:16:29.149
good thing. It might help with bone density,
in similar ways. But at the lining of

00:16:29.149 --> 00:16:32.990
the uterus, for many women it actually
acts as an anti-estrogen. So the

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:38.389
way she experiences that, is having very
light menses or no menses at all.

00:16:38.389 --> 00:16:43.370
So a lot of people watching this will be able
to recognize that, they'll be like yeah

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:47.059
when they're taking the pill they will
have lighter menses than usual. That

00:16:47.059 --> 00:16:50.329
actually can be, for some, that's a
feature not a bug. So for example, we're

00:16:50.329 --> 00:16:54.559
talking about pain. For some women
they're taking the pill because of pain,

00:16:54.559 --> 00:16:59.600
perhaps related to endometriosis. So
having lower estrogen activity of the

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:04.399
uterus is actually a great thing and for
many women having a 2-3 day

00:17:04.399 --> 00:17:07.880
menses, or 1-2 day menses,
might be preferable to having a heavy

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:12.409
4-7 day flow. So there's value
to it for some, but you have to

00:17:12.409 --> 00:17:15.829
acknowledge that those women who are
having lighter mensies are having less

00:17:15.829 --> 00:17:20.000
estrogenic activity to the uterus while
they're taking the pill.

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:26.059
Right. That does totally make sense. Do you see the same outcomes when we are

00:17:26.059 --> 00:17:30.500
comparing different forms of
contraception, like IUD, NuvaRing, birth

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:34.760
control pill? I'm sure a lot of my
followers are going to wonder if one is

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:38.000
